  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145794",
      "title": "Combining Pre-Fetching With Client-Side Fetching",
      "lectureOrder": 290,
      "videoOrder": 270,
      "sourceHash": "40e75a461195b49bca9e7ba93a3253cabc37aaaf561eafcee3fba521a539625a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.72,
          "en": "Now as a little bonus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.72,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "at the end of this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 9.3,
          "en": "I wanna combine client-side data fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.3,
          "end": 12.5,
          "en": "with server-side pre-rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.5,
          "end": 14.39,
          "en": "Not because we need it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.39,
          "end": 16.11,
          "en": "but because it can be a pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.11,
          "end": 19.14,
          "en": "which you do need in other kinds of applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.14,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "where you wanna pre-render a basic snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 25.65,
          "en": "and then still fetch the latest data from the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.65,
          "end": 28.65,
          "en": "and therefore that is a pattern you should also know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.65,
          "end": 30.75,
          "en": "And I'll stick to the last sales page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.75,
          "end": 34.34,
          "en": "Here we are already fetching data on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.34,
          "end": 37.8,
          "en": "Now I just wanna prepare some data on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.8,
          "end": 40.97,
          "en": "or during the build process as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.97,
          "end": 44.13,
          "en": "And therefore we can add one of the two main functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.13,
          "end": 49.1,
          "en": "we learned about getStaticProps or getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.1,
          "end": 53.35,
          "en": "And I'll go for getStaticProps to pre generate that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.35,
          "end": 57.222,
          "en": "during the build process and possibly revalidate it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.222,
          "end": 60.803,
          "en": "after deployment with the revalidate key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 64.954,
          "en": "So for this we export the async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.954,
          "end": 69.49,
          "en": "getStaticProps here, where we get a context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.49,
          "end": 72.78999999999999,
          "en": "which we don't need here though so I will omit it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.78999999999999,
          "end": 73.82,
          "en": "And then in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.82,
          "end": 77.55,
          "en": "I wanna also fetch the same data which I'm fetching here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.55,
          "end": 79.13,
          "en": "on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.13,
          "end": 83.96000000000001,
          "en": "Now for this, we now can't use the useSWR hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.96000000000001,
          "end": 88.1,
          "en": "because this is not a React component down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.1,
          "end": 91.46000000000001,
          "en": "GetStaticProps is not a React component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.46000000000001,
          "end": 94.5,
          "en": "and therefore we can't use hooks in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 97.53999999999999,
          "en": "We'll have to write ordinary fetch code instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.53999999999999,
          "end": 100.327,
          "en": "So I will grab this code here from the common that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.327,
          "end": 104.72,
          "en": "I'd use a fact function where we did fetch manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.72,
          "end": 107.34,
          "en": "and I'll copy that into getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.34,
          "end": 109.43,
          "en": "and commented back in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.43,
          "end": 112.15,
          "en": "Now get rid of the code where we set some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.15,
          "end": 115.92,
          "en": "we don't need that here, and we're almost good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.92,
          "end": 118.05,
          "en": "Now we're using fetch here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 120.13,
          "en": "and as I briefly mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.13,
          "end": 123.885,
          "en": "you can use fetch here in getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.885,
          "end": 126.46,
          "en": "and getServerSideProps as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.46,
          "end": 131.46,
          "en": "Next.js ensures that this also is available in this context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.57,
          "end": 132.963,
          "en": "So on the service side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.586,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "and then we just use it as we did above.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 139.54,
          "en": "We pass the response, transform the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.54,
          "end": 143.3,
          "en": "and now then once we're done transforming the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.3,
          "end": 146.82999999999998,
          "en": "here after this for loop, what now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.82999999999998,
          "end": 149.02,
          "en": "Well now you should keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.02,
          "end": 152.145,
          "en": "that the function you have here getsStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.145,
          "end": 153.62,
          "en": "is an async function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.62,
          "end": 155.787,
          "en": "So it wants a promise in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.787,
          "end": 158.54,
          "en": "And we do have a promise here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.54,
          "end": 160.68,
          "en": "So all I wanna do here in this second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.68,
          "end": 164.94,
          "en": "then block is return my object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.94,
          "end": 167.873,
          "en": "which eventually should be returned by getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.23,
          "end": 172.85,
          "en": "I will return an object with a props key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.85,
          "end": 174.95,
          "en": "where in there I have an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.95,
          "end": 179.64,
          "en": "with a key of sales, which holds my transform sales.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 183.35,
          "en": "And here we could then also add the revalidate key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.35,
          "end": 186.5,
          "en": "and set this to 10 seconds for example if we want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.5,
          "end": 188.28,
          "en": "so that as you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.28,
          "end": 191.15,
          "en": "this is executed again every 10 seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.15,
          "end": 195.223,
          "en": "or at most once every 10 seconds after deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 198.96,
          "en": "And now we just also need to return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.96,
          "end": 202.21,
          "en": "the overall promise chain by adding a return statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.21,
          "end": 204.2,
          "en": "here in front of fetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.2,
          "end": 207.78,
          "en": "so that the overall promise with all its step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.78,
          "end": 211.303,
          "en": "and the final data here is returned by getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.94,
          "end": 215.36,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could of course also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.36,
          "end": 217.46,
          "en": "use the await keyword here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.46,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "Then in the end we just would have written",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 223.743,
          "en": "response=await;fetch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.61,
          "end": 227.6,
          "en": "Then here we would write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.6,
          "end": 232.6,
          "en": "const data = await response.json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 235.1,
          "end": 237.69,
          "en": "and remove this semi colon here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.69,
          "end": 240.683,
          "en": "remove this, then block here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.641,
          "end": 244.36,
          "en": "And now we would be back to the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.36,
          "end": 246.51,
          "en": "you recognize from before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.51,
          "end": 249.54,
          "en": "So that is how we could write this with a single wait.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.54,
          "end": 253.26,
          "en": "Both works there is no better or worse alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.26,
          "end": 257.783,
          "en": "It's just different syntax for the exactly same operation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.37,
          "end": 262.73,
          "en": "So now we return our data as part of the props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.73,
          "end": 265.3,
          "en": "and therefore now here in the last sales page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.3,
          "end": 267.51,
          "en": "we of course should accept props again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.51,
          "end": 270.733,
          "en": "and do something with those sales we receive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.8,
          "end": 275.13,
          "en": "The question now just is what should we do with them?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.13,
          "end": 278.76,
          "en": "And I would say here, it makes by far the most sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.76,
          "end": 281.02,
          "en": "to use the props we get here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.02,
          "end": 286.02,
          "en": "the pre fetched and pre-rendered sales as our initial state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.2,
          "end": 291,
          "en": "So the initial state for the sales state is prop.sales,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291,
          "end": 293.53,
          "en": "those pre-rendered sales from the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.53,
          "end": 295.56,
          "en": "or from the build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.56,
          "end": 297.18,
          "en": "These are the sales which are used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.18,
          "end": 299.12,
          "en": "for the initial state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.12,
          "end": 301.52,
          "en": "They then can and will be overwritten",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.52,
          "end": 304.81,
          "en": "by the result of the client side data fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.81,
          "end": 306.75,
          "en": "But initially we use the sales,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 306.75,
          "end": 308.83,
          "en": "which we get from getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.83,
          "end": 312.023,
          "en": "as our state for the sales state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.01,
          "end": 315.022,
          "en": "And that means that now initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.022,
          "end": 318.2,
          "en": "this year will not return loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.2,
          "end": 321.67,
          "en": "because sales will not be undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 321.67,
          "end": 323.21,
          "en": "However, we should change this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.21,
          "end": 326.48,
          "en": "from an or to an end operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 326.48,
          "end": 329.35,
          "en": "If we don't have data and we don't have sales",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 329.35,
          "end": 331.6,
          "en": "then I wanna show loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 331.6,
          "end": 335.27,
          "en": "But now we do have sales because we pre-populate them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.27,
          "end": 338.67,
          "en": "We initialize our state with the pre fetched data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.67,
          "end": 339.763,
          "en": "from getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.95,
          "end": 343.32,
          "en": "So now we'll make it past this if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 343.32,
          "end": 346.22,
          "en": "and render our initial sales here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 346.22,
          "end": 348.7,
          "en": "So that's not what will be pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 348.7,
          "end": 352.02,
          "en": "And still when this component then runs in the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 352.02,
          "end": 355.093,
          "en": "it will fetch again to fetch the latest sales.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 356.5,
          "end": 361.5,
          "en": "So if I save this here and I reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 363.41,
          "end": 365.67,
          "en": "now we see what we saw before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 365.67,
          "end": 367.86,
          "en": "But if we view the page source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 367.86,
          "end": 371.07,
          "en": "we see now that our sales data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 371.07,
          "end": 373.89,
          "en": "is part of the pre-rendered page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 373.89,
          "end": 376.93,
          "en": "and that's a difference compared to before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 376.93,
          "end": 380.47,
          "en": "Now if we reload again and the data would have changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 380.47,
          "end": 383.36,
          "en": "between the point of time it was pre rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 383.36,
          "end": 386.39,
          "en": "and prepared and we visited this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 386.39,
          "end": 388.31,
          "en": "If the data would have changed here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 388.31,
          "end": 391.4,
          "en": "then we would see the updated data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 391.4,
          "end": 393.48,
          "en": "since it is fetched in the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 393.48,
          "end": 395.82,
          "en": "but not here in the page source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.82,
          "end": 398.51,
          "en": "Now that's hard to simulate here in development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 398.51,
          "end": 400.096,
          "en": "since this will always trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 400.096,
          "end": 402.61,
          "en": "getStaticProps for every visit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 402.61,
          "end": 407.61,
          "en": "but it's easier to show if I build this for production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 407.63,
          "end": 412.63,
          "en": "and I remove revalidate so that this is not revalidated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 412.65,
          "end": 414.8,
          "en": "after running it in production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 414.8,
          "end": 417.68,
          "en": "because that again will make it hard to kind of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 417.68,
